* **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS):** Mandatory 6-digit alphanumeric HUID hallmarking regulations enacted under the BIS Act 2016 (effective April 1, 2023) for 14K (585), 18K (750), and 22K (916) gold; verification via the official BIS Care App.
* **Gold Metallurgy & Tensile Strength:** 14K (58.5% pure gold) and 18K (75.0% pure gold) offer significantly superior yield strength and scratch resistance for lightweight daily earrings compared to soft 22K (91.6%).
* **Taxation & Hallmarking Fees:** Indian Goods and Services Tax (GST) rate of 3% applied uniformly to fine gold jewellery, with statutory ₹45 + 18% GST BIS hallmarking fee per item.

